 home  from the hospital all we gotta do is get  this one home but what you don't know  is the painful and challenging road this  couple endured  just to get to this very moment she was  growing  and i was breaking i was breaking apart  i could i couldn't move i couldn't walk  it was terrifying  it really was because i didn't know if i  was equipped to be able to deal with  all of those things as rj pulaski and  his wife take in the sunshine on the  back deck of their toronto home  there is a lot to be thankful for in the  summer of 2019  margaret received the best and worst  news possible  she was pregnant but one day later the  doctor found a lump on her breast  it was cancer and it spread throughout  her spine breaking vertebraes and ribs  not long after she would learn her  cancer was metastatic  i was just able to take things one day  at a time and just like okay  i'm here i'm here another day from worse  the worst the worst the worst to worse  and i think it was a lot of unknowns  another thing the couple didn't plan for  was marianna's early arrival  she was born at just 27 weeks at that  moment  r.j had a wife who was still undergoing  cancer treatments  and a baby in the neonatal intensive  care unit  at mount sinai hospital r.j quickly  graduated from husband to father  and began caring for both girls being  present  in those moments is the most important  thing  for for me for my time with my daughter  and my time with my wife  time that is limited margaret's cancer  is stable at the moment but the  prognosis  isn't good marianna is 17 months old now  and developing well  they spend every waking moment making  memories as a family  in isolation marianna choose hope  as something better for the future for  the next day for the next moment for the  next hour  i really do believe we did that like we  we did it and we're doing it and you can  see that hope when you watch this little  family of three  interact with each other it is a  reminder that hope  is a 